joining us right now is republican  congressman tony gonzalez his district  includes the city of uvalde texas  congressman good morning let's jump  right in you've been in touch with  officials there and last night you said  that there's still families waiting to  be connected with their children are  there still families um waiting to be  reunited  yeah good morning thank you for having  me you know it was such a horrific scene  that uh many of the children could not  be identified and they had to use dna  and other other avenues to identify  children so that's still ongoing i'll  get a briefing today at 10 30 there in  uvalde with all the latest details of it  along with governor abbott and senator  cornyn but imagine you're a parent and  you can't even identify your child so  this is what our community is dealing  with i am a parent i'm a father of six  and it hit me pretty hard yesterday and  you know as i was making my way my  district was very large as i was making  my way from el paso to the other side of  the district driving overnight yet  really let me process things and  not only do we have to think about the  victims we also have to think about the  survivors you know you mentioned you  know the board attack there were border  patrol agents these were the folks that  neutralized this shooter and ultimately  saved lives the stories i've heard where  there were there were a couple of  children that were hiding in a closet if  it wasn't for these agents uh you know  who knows what happened to those  children  i keep thinking about those children too  congressman the the children that didn't  survive and the ones that did  what they saw is something nobody should  see especially a little child but you  know you have voted against two gun gun  reform measures uh including one that  that called for expanded background  checks are you rethinking that position  this morning in light of what has  happened  in your in  happy to debate i'm happy to debate  policy uh not today i mean today we my  community is hurting you know  politicians like to divide us leaders  unite us and we need to be united right  now as americans because what happened  in uvalde texas can happen anywhere and  we have to be united in protecting our  children against that right now i've got  families that don't that can't identify  their children i've got folks that have  to bury their children i mean these are  the things that we're working with i'm  worried about the police officers that  came out of that scene covered in blood  that they have seen so much that they've  got to get pulled off of the front line  i'm worried about the community in  itself i'm happy to debate policy  another time but today we should be  united we should talk about the  survivors as well as well as the victims  i hear you loud and clear and i  certainly don't want to debate this and  i i too am thinking about the survivors  and the victims  but this is the issue this keeps  happening and we keep skirting around it  and we keep saying  somebody do something and nobody does  anything and we keep hearing it's the  second amendment rights the right to  bear arms and i keep thinking when the  founding fathers wrote that they were  talking about muskets i do not think if  if they were here today that they were  thinking that people kids would have  these assault rifles so if not now to  debate it if not not debate discuss it  right i just want to know you're in a  position but but with all due respect  you're in a position of power you're in  a position of power to change things  right and if we can't talk about it and  we can't make changes when can we talk  about it yeah to me this is a perfect  day to talk about you know i grew up in  camp wood texas you know very  30 40 miles from uvalde this is my home  you've audi isn't a dot on a map for me  it's not a political football for me  this is home these people i know these  are my community i represent them i love  them right now we need love we need  compassion we need people to come  together as we heal you ask what what  have we done and i'll give you we need  love but we need change congressman we  need change we need congress to come  together we need congress to come  together we need change  please  you've heard everybody say we don't need  the love and the prayers and the support  in the moment of silence they're saying  we're sick of that we don't need that  now i'm a man of faith my community is a  man  welcome your prayers let me let me give  an example of what we did last year so  the county judge who is a democrat the  mayor who is a republican and myself we  sat down over a year ago and you know  what we talked about we talked about  building a mental health clinic in  uvalde texas something that does not  exist and what did we do i used one of  my community projects and we allocated  two million dollars for this mental  health clinic it's a 20 million dollar  project i'm focused on how do i come up  with the other 18 million dollars if you  are a parent watching today i would say  reach out to your school find out what  your school's policies are find out what  mental health facilities are in your  area not only for your own family but  for others these are the things that  need that brings us together because  when tragedy hits  it doesn't determine if you're a  republican or democrat voted the club  right in who you pray to exactly this  country we need to come together dale  together not divide us  all of us need to come together and  focus on coming together though i think  is making change to keep the guns out of  people that should not be walking around  with  with and i don't want to take your guns  away from responsible gun owners nobody  wants to do that right but we've got to  go we've got to move people once full  safety but  just like every other father and mother  in america these are the conversations  that congress and others should be  having these conversations not the  division congress there's too much  division in this country yeah i agree  with you i agree with you and we thank  you tony gonzalez for taking the time to  spend time with us this morning

